@page "/"

<PageTitle>BbScanner samples</PageTitle>

<h1>BbScanner samples</h1>

<p>
    The same pages run in every Blazor hosting model: Server, WebAssembly, Auto and MAUI (Blazor Hybrid), and the
    scanner below opens the camera in each. What differs is where the frames come from and where .NET decodes them: on
    WebAssembly the browser's camera, decoded in the browser; on a Server circuit the browser's camera, each frame's
    searched region sent to the server; in the MAUI app the device's own camera, through Bit.BbScanner.Maui, straight
    to the decoder in the app. The <NavLink href="decoder">decoder</NavLink> reads barcodes in-process on every host.
</p>

<section>
    <h2>This host</h2>
    <HostFacts>
        <dt>Scanner</dt>
        <dd>@_status</dd>
        <dt>Frames decoded</dt>
        <dd>@_decoded@(_decoded > 0 ? $" ({_frame.DecodedWidth}x{_frame.DecodedHeight}, {_frame.Total.TotalMilliseconds:0.0} ms the last)" : "")</dd>
    </HostFacts>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Camera</h2>
    <p>
        Point the camera at a QR code, an EAN-13 or any other common symbology - the QR Code, Data Matrix, Code 128,
        Code 39, EAN, UPC and ITF symbols on the <NavLink href="decoder">decoder</NavLink> page, shown on another
        screen, will do. This scanner keeps to <code>BbBarcodeFormat.Common</code>, the default: PDF417, Aztec,
        MaxiCode, Micro QR, Codabar, Code 93 and GS1 DataBar each cost every frame time of their own, so an app asks
        for them by name through <code>Formats</code>, and the camera here passes them by. <em>Scan image</em> reads
        a photo instead, without opening the camera.
    </p>

    <div class="surface">
        <BbScanner @ref="_scanner"
                   Region="BbScanRegion.CenteredSquare(0.7)"
                   OnScan="HandleScan"
                   OnError="e => _error = e"
                   OnStatusChanged="s => _status = s"
                   OnDiagnostics="HandleDiagnostics" />
    </div>

    @if (_error is not null)
    {
        <p class="status error"><strong>@_error.Kind</strong>: @_error.Message</p>
    }

    <ResultList Results="_results" />
</section>

<section>
    <h2>What each page checks</h2>
    <ul class="features">
        <li>This page - the live camera: permission, the frame loop, the reticle and duplicate suppression.</li>
        <li><NavLink href="image">Images</NavLink> - a picked or dropped photo, Blazor's <code>InputFile</code>, and pixels the application already has.</li>
        <li><NavLink href="decoder">Decoder</NavLink> - <code>BbBarcodeDecoder</code> reading every symbology in-process, with the cost of a frame on this host.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

@code {
    private readonly List<BbBarcodeResult> _results = [];
    private BbScannerStatus _status = BbScannerStatus.Idle;
    private BbScanner? _scanner;
    private long _decoded;
    private BbScanDiagnostics _frame;

    // Twice a second at most: proof, on every host, that frames reach the decoder and what each one costs there.
    private void HandleDiagnostics(BbScanDiagnostics frame)
    {
        _frame = frame;
        _decoded = _scanner?.FramesDecoded ?? 0;
    }
    private BbScannerException? _error;

    private void HandleScan(BbBarcodeResult result)
    {
        _error = null;
        ResultList.Prepend(_results, [result]);
    }
}
